<title>SPAIN: Spanish retail sales rose 2.02 yr/yr in December.</title>
<headline>Spanish retail sales rose 2.02 yr/yr in December.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish retail sales data for December showed a 34.42 jump in December versus November, and a 2.02 percent rise versus the same month one year ago, the National Statistics Institute INE said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>INE gave the following breakdown:</p>
<p>				   VS NOV 96     VS DEC 95</p>
<p> General index		+34.42 pct	2.02 pct</p>
<p> Food			   +21.27 pct     -8.29 pct</p>
<p> Personal goods	     +32.78 pct	1.36 pct</p>
<p> Household goods	    +30.26 pct	4.14 pct</p>
<p> Other consumer goods     +68.09 pct     20.64 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Other consumer goods include toys and personal computers</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
